WEBVTT

02:44.289 --> 02:45.290
Nezuko!

02:46.541 --> 02:49.085
Stop chasing him. Come back here.

02:50.336 --> 02:51.629
Come back here now.

02:57.552 --> 02:58.553
Nezuko!

03:07.937 --> 03:12.483
Master Urokodaki once said
that Nezuko is already a demon.

03:13.985 --> 03:18.865
She's definitely not so weak
as to need my protection.

03:20.992 --> 03:23.286
Is it okay to rely on her?

03:24.662 --> 03:28.166
If she can protect them for me,
I can focus on attacking.

03:42.597 --> 03:43.640
Nezuko.

03:50.271 --> 03:52.565
Nezuko, I'm going down.

03:53.274 --> 03:54.901
You take good care of them.

03:58.655 --> 03:59.822
I know you can do it.

04:29.644 --> 04:30.979
I'm in a swamp.

04:33.273 --> 04:34.399
These are...

04:41.364 --> 04:44.617
The clothes and belongings
of those being taken away?

04:47.620 --> 04:50.790
They have claimed so many innocent lives.

04:51.666 --> 04:52.917
It's unforgivable.

04:55.461 --> 04:56.546
Truly unforgivable.

05:01.426 --> 05:03.511
Isn't it suffocating, brat?

05:03.720 --> 05:06.639
There's almost no air in this swamp

05:06.723 --> 05:11.644
and you must be feeling heavy
surrounded in its darkness.

05:13.730 --> 05:16.024
You're not as nimble as you are on land.

05:16.107 --> 05:17.233
Serves you right.

05:17.317 --> 05:21.029
It's stupid enough for you
to jump in so recklessly.

05:33.958 --> 05:35.335
Don't underestimate me.

05:35.668 --> 05:39.213
Where do you think I trained for this?

05:40.173 --> 05:43.885
The air in Sagiri Mountain
is much thinner than here.

05:51.559 --> 05:52.560
Besides...

05:54.145 --> 05:57.440
I have killer moves
that work best underwater.

06:09.243 --> 06:12.413
They can move at angles like this
in the swamp?

06:13.289 --> 06:14.582
But that doesn't matter.

06:15.083 --> 06:18.002
I can only attack them with my sword
when they come near.

06:18.753 --> 06:21.881
It's a move that I can use
even when I don't have a footing.

06:23.424 --> 06:26.552
By fiercely twisting
my upper and lower body,

06:26.677 --> 06:28.721
I'll create a massive whirlpool.

06:39.524 --> 06:40.566
I smell it.

06:40.733 --> 06:41.901
An opening thread.

06:42.610 --> 06:44.112
Total Concentration Breathing.

06:44.612 --> 06:46.114
Breath of Water!

06:46.781 --> 06:47.990
Sixth Form.

06:49.742 --> 06:51.285
Whirlpool!

07:23.693 --> 07:24.777
I can't take it.

07:25.403 --> 07:26.654
I've got to get up fast.

07:29.157 --> 07:30.283
Nezuko.

07:57.643 --> 07:59.729
This girl is strong.

08:03.858 --> 08:08.446
She hasn't used any mystical power
and she's already formidable.

08:09.071 --> 08:13.159
Perhaps she has consumed
a huge amount of blood.

08:19.916 --> 08:23.044
She moves so fast,
I can't get back in my swamp.

08:24.045 --> 08:28.716
But I'm already getting used to
such monotonous attacks!

08:33.137 --> 08:35.723
Even if she kicks my head off

08:36.182 --> 08:38.851
or blows out my guts,

08:38.935 --> 08:41.687
a demon like me can heal quickly!

08:51.155 --> 08:56.118
Good, now I'm going to punch
a hole in your face!

09:02.542 --> 09:04.335
Keep your hands off my sister!

09:20.309 --> 09:21.477
He killed them?

09:21.644 --> 09:24.564
Did he kill the other two?

09:29.026 --> 09:32.738
You three have the stench of rotten oil.

09:33.739 --> 09:35.324
It's extremely unbearable.

09:36.075 --> 09:38.494
How many people have you killed?

09:38.869 --> 09:45.167
If we let those girls live on,
they will grow ugly and stale.

09:45.459 --> 09:47.336
So we ate them for their own good!

09:49.839 --> 09:52.508
You should thank us demons for--

09:58.097 --> 09:59.223
That's enough.

10:06.564 --> 10:10.151
Tell me what you know
about Muzan Kibutsuji.

10:27.168 --> 10:28.461
Tell me everything.

10:30.338 --> 10:31.422
Tell me!

10:33.549 --> 10:34.717
I can't.

10:40.431 --> 10:41.724
I can't tell you.

10:45.061 --> 10:46.854
Don't tell anyone.

10:49.190 --> 10:52.360
Never tell anyone about me at all.

10:55.988 --> 11:01.243
I'll know right away if you do
because I'm always watching you.

11:04.163 --> 11:07.375
I can't tell you, I can't!

11:08.292 --> 11:09.835
I can't.

11:11.045 --> 11:15.049
It's the scent of him so scared
that his bones are trembling deep inside.

11:17.259 --> 11:19.970
I can't tell you!

11:36.946 --> 11:39.782
Again, I failed to gather information.

11:47.581 --> 11:48.541
Nezuko!

11:55.089 --> 11:56.257
She's asleep.

11:57.174 --> 11:58.551
She has stopped bleeding.

11:59.051 --> 12:00.928
Is she sleeping to recover?

12:07.601 --> 12:11.272
I'm sorry,
but you have to wait a little longer.

12:11.897 --> 12:15.109
I promise I'll turn you back into a human.

12:40.259 --> 12:41.260
Mr. Kazumi.

12:42.720 --> 12:43.971
Are you all right?

12:47.224 --> 12:49.018
I lost my fiancée.

12:50.269 --> 12:51.979
Do you think I'm all right?

12:57.735 --> 12:58.861
Mr. Kazumi.

13:01.489 --> 13:04.033
No matter how much you have lost,

13:04.575 --> 13:06.202
life must go on.

13:07.870 --> 13:09.830
No matter how tough it gets,
you have to move on.

13:12.875 --> 13:14.460
What do you know?

13:14.710 --> 13:16.629
You're just a kid,
you don't know anything!

13:36.273 --> 13:37.650
I'm about to leave now.

13:41.111 --> 13:42.154
For you.

13:45.115 --> 13:48.953
I believe that they are
Ms. Satoko's belongings.

14:11.600 --> 14:13.561
You've been through
something like this too?

14:14.353 --> 14:15.646
Is that what you mean?

14:20.317 --> 14:22.486
I... I'm sorry!

14:22.903 --> 14:24.446
I said horrible things to you.

14:24.613 --> 14:26.240
Please forgive me.

14:27.616 --> 14:28.826
I'm really sorry!

14:35.165 --> 14:36.667
His scar-ridden hands...

14:37.251 --> 14:39.545
have grown tougher and thicker
through intensive training.

14:41.297 --> 14:43.257
Those aren't the hands of a boy.

14:45.217 --> 14:48.095
I'll leave the young lady to you.

14:50.890 --> 14:52.016
I got it!

14:53.809 --> 14:54.852
I got it.

15:10.868 --> 15:12.202
It's not only me.

15:13.704 --> 15:15.539
How many people have you killed?

15:15.789 --> 15:18.083
How many people
have you caused torment and suffering?

15:19.919 --> 15:21.420
Muzan Kibutsuji,

15:22.254 --> 15:25.549
I'll never forgive you for this!

15:34.808 --> 15:38.062
Next stop is Asakusa, Tokyo.

15:38.270 --> 15:41.148
Rumor has it
that demons are lurking there.

15:43.651 --> 15:45.152
Do I have to go there right away?

15:45.235 --> 15:47.071
Right away.

15:47.821 --> 15:49.573
Wait a second.

15:49.698 --> 15:51.241
No.

15:51.325 --> 15:55.704
-Just give me a couple of seconds...
-No, stop grumbling and start moving.

16:16.809 --> 16:20.145
The city has developed so much.

16:20.229 --> 16:21.897
It's so bright at night.

16:30.739 --> 16:32.324
The buildings are so tall!

16:32.700 --> 16:33.909
What is that?

16:35.160 --> 16:38.372
So this is what they call a metropolis.

16:48.674 --> 16:50.175
My head is spinning.

16:53.887 --> 16:55.222
Let's go there, Nezuko.

16:58.684 --> 17:00.310
Sorry for bothering you!

17:17.953 --> 17:19.997
UDON

17:20.122 --> 17:21.498
Excuse me, sir.

17:22.750 --> 17:25.085
Can I have yam udon noodles?

17:25.377 --> 17:26.754
Sure, right away.

17:34.344 --> 17:36.764
This is my first time here.

17:37.347 --> 17:38.807
There were too many people.

17:47.066 --> 17:50.152
Here is your bowl of yam udon noodles.

17:50.652 --> 17:52.154
Thank you, kind sir.

18:28.232 --> 18:29.399
This smell...

18:30.067 --> 18:32.152
Why did it suddenly appear
in a place like this?

18:39.993 --> 18:41.745
It's the scent he left at my house.

18:46.250 --> 18:47.793
It's Muzan Kibutsuji.

18:51.505 --> 18:53.841
It's his scent!

19:08.939 --> 19:10.232
It's him!

19:11.775 --> 19:12.776
Dad.

19:17.823 --> 19:18.949
Who are you?

19:21.410 --> 19:25.455
-He...
-It's okay, don't be afraid.

19:26.665 --> 19:29.126
He's living in disguise as a human.

19:31.503 --> 19:33.672
Why would you like to see me?

19:34.423 --> 19:36.967
You seem to be in a state of panic.

19:38.135 --> 19:39.887
What's the matter?

19:40.512 --> 19:41.638
Mom.

19:51.231 --> 19:52.441
They are humans.

19:53.942 --> 19:56.904
The scent from the girl
and the woman are humans.

19:59.448 --> 20:00.699
Aren't they aware of it?

20:01.450 --> 20:02.784
Don't they even know...

20:03.952 --> 20:05.412
that he's a demon?

20:06.747 --> 20:08.290
He's a man-eating demon.

20:10.167 --> 20:11.627
Do you know him?

20:12.127 --> 20:13.253
No.

20:14.087 --> 20:16.381
It's really puzzling me.

20:17.674 --> 20:19.718
I've never seen this young man before.

20:23.055 --> 20:26.308
Maybe he mistook me for someone else.

20:27.267 --> 20:29.102
I see.

20:36.068 --> 20:38.320
Are you okay, honey?

20:46.578 --> 20:47.704
Honey?

20:51.708 --> 20:52.751
Stop!

22:41.860 --> 22:43.779
Finally, I found Muzan Kibutsuji.

22:43.987 --> 22:46.114
I just need to defeat him
to turn you back into a human.

22:47.616 --> 22:51.453
That being said, the Asakusa folks
are really fashionable.

22:52.454 --> 22:54.289
You'll look great dressing up like them.

22:54.748 --> 22:57.459
In the meantime, here's a little
gossip from the Taisho era.

22:57.876 --> 23:00.754
Mr. Toyo, the udon seller
is born and bred in Asakusa.

23:00.837 --> 23:04.841
I heard that he loves Asakusa so much,
so that's where he set up his udon stall.

23:06.468 --> 23:07.761
Me in a suit?

23:07.844 --> 23:09.638
That will make me look more grown-up.

23:10.305 --> 23:11.973
I have to get back to my mission.

23:12.224 --> 23:15.018
Next, episode 8,
"The Smell of Enchanting Blood."

23:15.352 --> 23:16.603
TO BE CONTINUED

23:16.686 --> 23:18.063
Subtitle translation by CL Tan
